{"uuid": "01d53e49-7833-4122-a970-b72c73ad2c28", "variant": "base", "mode": "judged", "verdict": "pass", "notes": "as player, desktop: playable from hand; the Choose one prompt from Crimson Pilgrimage is cancellable and names both modes from the card text; choosing the ephemeral mode opens the private gallery 'Draw 2 cards' (0/2 selected, Submit) over exactly the top 4 deck cards, labeled Your Deck, not cancellable; a reload restores the same prompt and candidates; the two drawn cards land in hand with the Ephemeral duration badge, the other two stay on top in their order; the log reads that you looked at the top 4 cards of your deck, then each draw; no clipping, __caps empty", "bead": "hv-umm2.58", "commit": "e49920e4cbb0086339037972013885f713d559dc", "screens": ["crimson-mode-desktop.png", "crimson-pick-desktop.png", "crimson-selected-desktop.png", "crimson-settled-desktop.png", "crimson-log-desktop.png"]}
{"uuid": "01d53e49-7833-4122-a970-b72c73ad2c28", "variant": "base", "mode": "judged", "verdict": "fail", "notes": "as player, mobile: the engine behavior, the private 'Draw a card' gallery (draw-1 mode), the reload, the draw, and the log are right, but in the Choose one prompt the held Crimson Pilgrimage card (the play awaiting its mode, at the left of the near hand row) covers the left ~65 px of the wrapped second option 'Draw 2 of the cards and they gain ephemeral', hiding the start of its label (elementFromPoint at 3-15% of the button's width hits the card); the cause is the battle screen's choice-prompt controls layout beside the pending play's card, outside this bead's areas; a fix bead is needed", "bead": "hv-umm2.58", "commit": "e49920e4cbb0086339037972013885f713d559dc", "screens": ["crimson-mode-mobile.png", "crimson-mode-overlap-mobile.png", "crimson-pick-mobile.png", "crimson-settled-mobile.png", "crimson-log-mobile.png"]}
{"uuid": "01d53e49-7833-4122-a970-b72c73ad2c28", "variant": "base", "mode": "judged", "verdict": "pass", "notes": "as enemy, desktop and mobile: the AI plays it, chooses a mode, looks, and draws; the human's log reads that the opponent played Crimson Pilgrimage and looked at the top 4 cards of their deck, without naming any looked-at or drawn card; the undrawn cards stay on top of the AI's deck in order; __caps empty", "bead": "hv-umm2.58", "commit": "e49920e4cbb0086339037972013885f713d559dc", "screens": ["crimson-enemy-start-desktop.png", "crimson-enemy-settled-desktop.png", "crimson-enemy-log-desktop.png", "crimson-enemy-start-mobile.png", "crimson-enemy-settled-mobile.png", "crimson-enemy-log-mobile.png"]}
